        "Mehran Kardar",
        "Yi-Cheng Zhang",
        "Kazumasa A. Takeuchi"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The KPZ universality class identifies a simple mechanism and robust scaling laws for stochastic growth, with reach well beyond its original model.",
        "attribution": "Kardar and Zhang established the central theoretical framework; Takeuchi's experiments provided striking quantitative tests of its universal predictions.",
        "maturity": "Theoretical development and experimental confirmation make this a mature, well-tested result.",
        "uncertainties": [
